stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> awaiting_forge : dream creates brief [kind = new | replace | extend]
    [*] --> awaiting_user : dream creates brief [kind = deprecate]
    awaiting_forge --> awaiting_user : tool propose submit [requirements + tool.md + source + path lint pass]
    awaiting_forge --> awaiting_forge : tool propose submit [path lint fails]
    awaiting_user --> approved : tool propose approve
    awaiting_user --> rejected : tool propose reject
    approved --> [*]
    rejected --> [*] : rejected count for pattern_key < 3
    rejected --> [*] : rejected count for pattern_key = 3 (pattern blacklisted)

    note right of awaiting_user
        On submit: attach hardened
        requirement, tool.md, source, optional tests,
        dependencies, and correctness argument.
        deprecate briefs skip forge: there is
        no source to harden, so they enter
        awaiting_user directly and submit is
        rejected for them.
    end note

    note right of approved
        Side effects branch on kind.
        new: registry insert + tool.md + install.
        replace / extend: lineage update +
        tool.md + swap, predecessor to .history/.
        deprecate: registry status -> disabled +
        archive binary; no tool.md, no install.
        All in one DB transaction; no memory
        write participates. Filesystem work
        follows the registry mutation protocol.
    end note

    note left of rejected
        Blacklist is a dream-side guard:
        count terminal rejected rows for
        the same pattern_key before
        drafting. Derived, not stored.
    end note
